
/*! \page SerialPort_dox Serial port library
 *
 * \section SerialPort_VariousInfoSandbox Various info sandbox
 *
 * \subsection _ DTE and DCE
 *
 * In the world of serial communications, there are two different kinds of equipment:
 * |Abbreviation|Name                              |Examples|
 * |:----------:|:---------------------------------|:-------|
 * | DTE        |Data Terminal Equipment           |PC      |
 * | DCE        |Data Circuit-terminating Equipment|Modem   |
 * | ^          |Data Communication Equipment      |^       |
 *
 * \sa https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Serial_Programming/RS-232_Connections#Data_Terminal/Communications_Equipment
 * \sa https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Serial_port#DTE_and_DCE
 *
 *
 * \subsection _ Data and control signals
 *
 * \sa https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/RS-232#Data_and_control_signals
 * \sa https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Serial_port#Pinouts
 * \sa https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Serial_Programming/RS-232_Connections#Wiring_Pins_Explained
 *
 * 
 * 
 * HW pinning
 * 
 * 
 * https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Serial_Programming/RS-232_Connections#Wiring_Pins_Explained
 *
 * |9-pin|25-pin|Definition               |Direction (PC view)|
 * |:---:|:----:|:------------------------|:------------------|
 * |  1  |  8   |DCD (Data Carrier Detect)| IN                |
 * |  2  |  3   |RX (Receive Data)        | IN                |
 * |  3  |  2   |TX (Transmit Data)       | OUT               |
 * |  4  |  20  |DTR (Data Terminal Ready)| OUT               |
 * |  5  |  7   |GND (Signal Ground)      | --                |
 * |  6  |  6   |DSR (Data Set Ready)     | IN                |
 * |  7  |  4   |RTS (Request To Send)    | OUT               |
 * |  8  |  5   |CTS (Clear To Send)      | IN                |
 * |  9  |  22  |RI (Ring Indicator)      | IN                |
 *
 * 
 * 
 * Control signals
 * 
 * https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/RS-232#Data_and_control_signals
 * 
 * |Abbreviation|Name               |Typical purpose                                                                       |Direction     |
 * |:----------:|:------------------|:-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|:------------:|
 * |    RTS     |Request To Send    |DTE requests the DCE prepare to transmit data                                         |DTE &rarr; DCE|
 * |    CTS     |Clear To Send      |DCE is ready to accept data from the DTE                                              |DTE &larr; DCE|
 * |    DCD     |Data Carrier Detect|DCE is receiving a carrier from a remote DCE                                          |DTE &larr; DCE|
 * |    DSR     |Data Set Ready     |DCE is ready to receive and send data                                                 |DTE &larr; DCE|
 * |    DTR     |Data Terminal Ready|DTE is ready to receive, initiate, or continue a call                                 |DTE &rarr; DCE|
 * |    RI      |Ring Indicator     |DCE has detected an incoming ring signal on the telephone line                        |DTE &larr; DCE|
 * |    RTR     |Ready To Receive   |DTE is ready to receive data from DCE. If in use, RTS is assumed to be always asserted|DTE &rarr; DCE|
 * 
 * https://doc.qt.io/qt-6/qserialport.html#PinoutSignal-enum
 * 
 * Test bridge plug
 * 
 * |pin|Designation   |
 * |:-:|:-------------|
 * |3-2|TX &rarr; RX  |
 * |7-8|RTS &rarr; CTS|
 * |4-6|DTR &rarr; DSR|
 * 
 * QSerialPort::PinoutSignals
 * 
 * For data, store a TX byte + RX byte ? NO!! just a bool !
 * 
 * See bytesWritten() and readyRead()
 * 
 * Timestamp ? Not here !
 * Timestamp should be in a deticaed, like ControlAndDataSignalsLogItem
 * 
 * - ControlAndDataSignals
 * - ControlAndDataSignalsModel (not an item model.. must handle signal emission as some point in time, do not spam the UI)
 * - ControlAndDataSignalsController  better than model ? No, model is more common in Qt..
 * - ControlAndDataSignalsWidget
 * 
 * I think PinoutSignals is better (our variant also adds TX/RX)
 * - PinoutSignals
 * - PinoutSignalsModel OR Controller ?
 * - PinoutSignalsWidgets
 * 
 * \todo Maybe add some definitions and there names from various source. Could help to choose a name.
 * 
 * \sa https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/RS-232
 * \sa https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Serial_port
 * \sa https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Serial_Programming/RS-232_Connections
 *
 * \section SerialPort_Errors Serial port errors
 *
 * \startuml "Exceptions"
 * !include ClassDiagrams/SerialPortExceptions.puml
 * \enduml
 *
 * \sa Mdt::SerialPort::FileOpenError
 * \sa Mdt::SerialPort::PortSetupError
 *
 *
 * \section SerialPort_PortInfo Serial port info
 *
 * Getting informations about available serial ports.
 *
 * QSerialPortInfo provides information about existing serial ports.
 *
 * To list the available serial ports, for example in a QComboBox
 * (or maybe in a QTableView),
 * the Mdt::SerialPort::PortInfoListTableModel can be used.
 *
 * While QSerialPortInfo can only be constructed for an existing port on the system,
 * we have to be able to test the access model without any port available (f.ex. CI):
 *
 * \startuml "Serial port info list table model"
 * !include ClassDiagrams/SerialPortInfoListTableModel.puml
 * \enduml
 *
 * \sa https://doc.qt.io/qt-6/qserialportinfo.html
 * \sa Mdt::SerialPort::PortInfoListTableModel
 *
 * \section SerialPort_Interface Serial port interface
 *
 *
 * \sa Mdt::SerialPort::Interface
 * \sa Mdt::SerialPort::InterfaceList
 *
 * \section SerialPort_SettingsList_TableModels Serial port settings list table models
 *
 * \todo Talk about attributes enumerations, available ports, etc..
 *
 * \todo Also talk about available table models
 *
 * \sa Mdt::SerialPort::BaudRateListTableModel
 * \sa Mdt::SerialPort::DataBitsListTableModel
 * \sa Mdt::SerialPort::FlowControlListTableModel
 * \sa Mdt::SerialPort::ParityListTableModel
 * \sa Mdt::SerialPort::StopBitsListTableModel
 * \sa Mdt::SerialPort::InterfaceListTableModel
 *
 * \section SerialPort_Settings Serial port settings
 *
 * Settings is a set of attributes required to open a serial port.
 *
 * \startuml "Serial port settings overview"
 * !include ClassDiagrams/SerialPortSettingsOverview.puml
 * \enduml
 *
 * \startuml "Serial port settings editor"
 * !include ClassDiagrams/SettingsEditor.puml
 * \enduml
 *
 * \sa Mdt::SerialPort::Settings
